==English==

===Etymology===
Back-formation from {{m|en|upholsterer|t=tradesman who finishes furniture}}, from {{inh|en|enm|upholdester}}, from {{der|en|enm|upholder|t=dealer in small goods}}, from {{m|enm|upholden|t=to repair, uphold}}; equivalent to {{af|en|uphold|-ster}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/əˈpɒl.stə(ɹ)/|/əˈpɐl.stə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fit]] [[padding]], [[stuffing]], [[spring]]s, [[webbing]] and [[fabric]] [[covering]] to ([[furniture]]).

